          ],
          "content": "Reprint 2026-27"
        },
        {
          "type": "header",
          "bbox": [
            0.24,
            0.095,
            0.736,
            0.123
          ],
          "content": "Q U E S T I O N S"
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph_title",
          "bbox": [
            0.101,
            0.137,
            0.666,
            0.154
          ],
          "level": 2,
          "content": "1. How is the process of pollination different from fertilisation?"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.099,
            0.156,
            0.699,
            0.173
          ],
          "content": "**2. What is the role of the seminal vesicles and the prostate gland?**"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.099,
            0.174,
            0.654,
            0.191
          ],
          "content": "**3. What are the changes seen in girls at the time of puberty?**"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.099,
            0.192,
            0.708,
            0.21
          ],
          "content": "**4. How does the embryo get nourishment inside the mother’s body?**"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.099,
            0.211,
            0.749,
            0.243
          ],
          "content": "**5. If a woman is using a copper -T, will it help in protecting her from sexually transmitted diseases?**"
        },
        {
          "type": "image",
          "bbox": [
            0.776,
            0.137,
            0.856,
            0.235
          ],
          "content": "",
          "captions": [],
          "footnotes": [],
          "image_source": "images/page_13_image_7.jpg"
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph_title",
          "bbox": [
            0.134,
            0.278,
            0.514,
            0.306
          ],
          "level": 2,
          "content": "What you have learnt"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.116,
            0.328,
            0.866,
            0.361
          ],
          "content": "n **Reproduction, unlike other life processes, is not essential to maintain the life of an individual organism.**"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.116,
            0.364,
            0.864,
            0.397
          ],
          "content": "n **Reproduction involves creation of a DNA copy and additional cellular apparatus by the cell involved in the process.**"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.116,
            0.399,
            0.864,
            0.434
          ],
          "content": "n **Various organisms use different modes of reproduction depending on their body design.**"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.116,
            0.436,
            0.864,
            0.469
          ],
          "content": "n **In fission, many bacteria and protozoa simply divide into two or more daughter cells.**"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.116,
            0.472,
            0.864,
            0.505
          ],
          "content": "n **Organisms such as hydra can regenerate if they are broken into pieces. They can also give out buds which mature into new individuals.**"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.116,
            0.508,
            0.864,
            0.541
          ],
          "content": "n **Roots, stems and leaves of some plants develop into new plants through vegetative propagation.**"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.116,
            0.544,
            0.863,
            0.577
          ],
          "content": "n **These are examples of asexual reproduction where new generations are created from a single individual.**"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.116,
            0.579,
            0.863,
            0.597
          ],
          "content": "n **Sexual reproduction involves two individuals for the creation of a new individual.**"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.116,
            0.6,
            0.864,
            0.649
          ],
          "content": "DNA copying mechanisms creates variations which are useful for ensuring the **survival of the species. Modes of sexual reproduction allow for greater variation to be generated.**"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.116,
            0.651,
            0.864,
            0.685
          ],
          "content": "n **Reproduction in flowering plants involves transfer of pollen grains from the anther to the stigma which is referred to as pollination. This is followed by fertilisation.**"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.116,
            0.687,
            0.864,
            0.721
          ],
          "content": "n **Changes in the body at puberty, such as increase in breast size in girls and new facial hair growth in boys, are signs of sexual maturation.**"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.116,
            0.723,
            0.864,
            0.757
          ],
          "content": "n **The male reproductive system in human beings consists of testes which produce sperms, vas deferens, seminal vesicles, prostate gland, urethra and penis.**"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.116,
            0.759,
            0.864,
            0.793
          ],
          "content": "n **The female reproductive system in human beings consists of ovaries, fallopian tubes, uterus and vagina.**"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.116,
            0.794,
            0.864,
            0.829
          ],
          "content": "n **Sexual reproduction in human beings involves the introduction of sperm in the vagina of the female. Fertilisation occurs in the fallopian tube.**"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.116,
            0.83,
            0.864,
            0.866
          ],
          "content": "Contraception to avoid pregnancy can be achieved by the use of condoms, oral **pills, copper-T and other methods.**"
        },
        {
          "type": "page_number",
          "bbox": [
            0.09,
